BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Puppy Kindergarten (Rachel Simmons)
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261129T151500Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261129T161000Z
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261108T010033Z
UID:1795965300_PuppyKindergarten@luckydog
DESCRIPTION:If you recently added a new puppy to your family\, you're in t
 he right place! Puppy Kindergarten is the perfect place to start for puppi
 es between the age of 2 and 5 months. We'll cover everything from teaching
  your puppy his name to the manners he'll need to be a great member of you
 r household. We'll also address unwanted behaviors like chewing\, jumping\
 , and pulling on the leash. Last but not least\, we'll help you socialize 
 your puppy to strange noises\, objects\, and surfaces!
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Trick Dog 1 -  Novice (Lea Pfeiffer)
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261129T151500Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261129T161000Z
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261108T010033Z
UID:1795965300_TrickDog1-Novice@luckydog
DESCRIPTION:This six-week class is designed to work towards your AKC Trick
  Dog Novice title! Teams will work on tricks for their respective levels i
 n stations.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Agility - Competition Level 1 (Beth Martin)
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261129T161500Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261129T171500Z
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261108T010033Z
UID:1795968900_Agility-CompetitionLevel1@luckydog
DESCRIPTION:Teams will continue building skills from previous courses. Tea
 ms must be able to perform:\nAll equipment\nContacts full height\nunassist
 ed see-saw\nClosed\n12 weaves without assistance\nCan utilize front\, rear
 \, and blind crosses on course\nRunning full courses at Novice to Open Lev
 els\nPinwheels\, serpentines\, and threadles\nProficient back sides and ju
 mp wraps\nNovice sends (6-10 ft gamble lines)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Manners 1 - Basic (Rachel Simmons)
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261129T163000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261129T172500Z
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261108T010033Z
UID:1795969800_Manners1-Basic@luckydog
DESCRIPTION:Let’s face it\, dogs these days are part of the family. But 
 as much as we treat them like furry humans\, they need some help to act li
 ke it! In Basic Manners\, we cover the essentials that your dog needs to b
 e a well-behaved member of your family. You’ll learn things like not jum
 ping up\, coming when called\, and walking nicely on a leash\, as well as 
 your standard sit\, down\, and stay! We also work on impulse control\, the
  “place” behavior\, and sitting at the door\, all of which discourage 
 naughty behavior like stealing food\, darting out the door\, and begging/c
 ounter surfing.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rally 0 - Intro (Lea Pfeiffer)
DTSTART;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261129T163000Z
DTEND;TZID=UTC;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261129T172500Z
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20261108T010033Z
UID:1795969800_Rally0-Intro@luckydog
DESCRIPTION:Looking for a fun way to build more focus with your dog? Wheth
 er you are preparing to take a Canine Good Citizen test\, Therapy Test or 
 maybe you just want to try something new…Rally helps you build a great f
 oundation with your dog and can help you in many other teamwork events.  
 This class refines your dogs basic manners and has real life applications.
   This class will focus on AKC Rally-O including attentive heeling\, fini
 sh\, fronts and some cone work. We use positive training techniques in a f
 un and supportive environment.\nPrerequisite: Successful completion of Man
 ners 2
END:VEVENT
